{"name":"Pastel China","hex":"#f0e4e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pastel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several subdued tints of colors, usually associated with pink, peach, yellow, green, blue, and lavender.","A drawing made with any of those colors."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional dish in various Latin American countries and in Indonesia, resembling a tamale, pasty, or calzone.","A Filipino stew made with vegetables, sausages, and chicken or other meat in a creamy sauce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastel"},{"term":"china","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of porcelain, a hard white translucent ceramic made from kaolin, now  sometimes distinguished in reference to tableware as fine or good china.","Chinaware: porcelain tableware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china"}],"entries":[{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China","wikidata":"Q148"},{"title":"Pastel","blocks":[{"text":"A pastel is an art medium that consists of powdered pigment and a binder. It can exist in a variety of forms, including a stick, a square, a pebble, and a pan of color, among other forms. The pigments used in pastels are similar to those used to produce some other colored visual arts media, such as oil paints; the binder is of a neutral hue and low saturation. The color effect of pastels is closer to the natural dry pigments than that of any other process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg/330px-William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel","wikidata":"Q189085"},{"title":"Pastel (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Pastels or pastel colors belong to a pale family of colors, which, when described in the HSV color space, have high value and low or medium saturation. They are named after the artistic medium made from pigment and solid binding agents, similar to crayons. Pastel sticks historically had lower saturation than paints of the same pigment, hence the name of this color family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Commercial_pastels.JPG/330px-Commercial_pastels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel_(color)","wikidata":"Q2513175"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/1280px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb